  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically queried the workspace multiple times, extracted key admission diagnoses (severe asphyxia, HIE, shock, sepsis, thrombocytopenia, coagulopathy) and later normalized PCT/platelets, clarified that inpatient antibiotics/hemostatics were stopped and not for home use, reconciled the unexpectedly found iron syrup, gave a concrete follow-up plan with an owner (neonatal follow-up clinic) and timing (within 7 days), and obtained caregiver receipt of red flags and next steps across several turns. No serious responsibility-chain error occurred; all minimum safety duties were met. However, the trajectory does not convincingly complete any case-defined high-order test point beyond minimum safe duties: the delayed result confusion was partially resolved, but the model did not actively reprioritize based on new symptoms, did not earn full high-order credit for preventing false-positive/false-negative errors, and the handoff repair was already required for safety. Therefore the maximum possible grade is 3 (Acceptable).",
